+## 🎯 Project Overview
+
+Pulseboard is a small web product for team facilitators who lose proposed action items after weekly meetings. A facilitator uploads a meeting transcript, reviews the action items Pulseboard extracts, and explicitly confirms an owner and due date for each item before that item can enter reminder scheduling. The product makes accountability visible while preventing unreviewed AI suggestions or autonomous messages from becoming team commitments.
+
+## 🎨 Project Type & Scale
+
+**Type**: Web Application (browser-based, responsive)
+
+**Estimated Scale**: Level 2 — a focused pilot with one core workflow, two user roles, transcript processing, and controlled reminder scheduling.
+
+**Primary Domain**: Enterprise/B2B team collaboration and action-item accountability.
+
+**Domain Expertise Required**: No — the brief describes a general workplace workflow; privacy, security, and reminder-channel decisions still need clarification before implementation.
+
+## 🚀 Vision & Goals
+
+### Vision Statement
+
+A world where team facilitators can turn a meeting transcript into owned, time-bound actions without letting uncertain suggestions or automated messages create commitments.
+
+### Primary Goals
+
+1. **Review completion**: At least 80% of proposed action items are reviewed during the five-team pilot.
+   - Success looks like: facilitators either confirm or deliberately decline most extracted suggestions.
+   - Key metric: reviewed proposed items ÷ all proposed items.
+
+2. **Accountability improvement**: Reduce unowned overdue actions by 30% after four weeks.
+   - Success looks like: teams have materially fewer past-due actions without a named owner.
+   - Key metric: count of unowned overdue actions, compared with the pilot baseline.
+
+3. **Human confirmation before reminders**: No reminder is schedulable until its action has a facilitator-confirmed owner and due date.
+   - Success looks like: the product rejects or withholds scheduling for incomplete or unconfirmed action items.
+   - Key metric: number of scheduled reminders lacking a confirmed owner or due date; target: zero.
+
